      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Hi, thanks for your report. It is by design that these random values are locally calculated by each client, as the option is intended for situations where syncing over the network isn't necessary.\n\nTo get the effect you're looking for, you can use a VRCAvatarParameterDriver to randomly set a network synced animator parameter and then use that to play an audio clip, like in the screenshot below.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-11-05T16:33:43.132Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I have a prop with an audio source with a VRC Animator Play Audio script and anytime an audio clip is \"randomly\" chosen and played, it's not the same audio clip to anyone who listens to it. So i.e. the prop plays sound 1 for me locally, friend A hears sound 2, another friend hears sound 4. As I think that's not intended, I would think the \"random\" playback order should choose a single random sound clip, which is the same clip heard by everyone who's in the vicinity.",
